From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Subject: media: cedrus: offer 10-bit AFBC capture for AVS2

10-bit AVS2 already reconstructs into a 10-bit AFBC surface behind its
P010 output, but AFBC itself could not be selected as the capture
format for an AVS2 source, as it can for H.265 and VP9. The vendor
library decodes 4K AVS2 into AFBC on this decoder, and on the H616 the
P010 secondary write limits a 4K Main10 stream to just under 60 fps
while the compressed output alone has headroom.

Add YUV420_10_AFBC_16X16_SPLIT as an opt-in capture format for 10-bit
AVS2, after the plain formats so that P010 stays the default. The AVS2
code already programs the single-plane AFBC addresses for the current
picture and the references, the AFBC VE_MODE bits and the HIGH10
10-bit configuration the vendor uses when no P010 output is enabled.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_video.c
+++ b/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_video.c
@@ -163,6 +163,19 @@
 		.depth		= 8,
 		.src_format	= V4L2_PIX_FMT_VP9_FRAME,
 	},
+	/*
+	 * 10-bit AVS2 into AFBC, as the vendor library does at 4K. Opt-in
+	 * like the VP9 entries: P010 (with the same AFBC reconstruction
+	 * behind it) stays the default 10-bit capture format.
+	 */
+	{
+		.pixelformat	= V4L2_PIX_FMT_YUV420_10_AFBC_16X16_SPLIT,
+		.directions	= CEDRUS_DECODE_DST,
+		.capabilities	= CEDRUS_CAPABILITY_UNTILED |
+				  CEDRUS_CAPABILITY_AVS2_DEC,
+		.depth		= 10,
+		.src_format	= V4L2_PIX_FMT_AVS2_FRAME,
+	},
 };
 
 #define CEDRUS_FORMATS_COUNT	ARRAY_SIZE(cedrus_formats)
